The decisive issue is now clear: Sections 4–7 do not pose a hard search problem; they give algebraic edge-set formulas and prove those formulas partition the torus/hypercube edges. The only unsolved regime is an existence/classification question, and the paper supplies neither a hardness result nor an inverse construction there. I’m recording an early rejection rather than fabricating passing gates or an oracle transcript.
